      "text": "We got a bunch of cards in various monetary value for Christmas gifts. Never ever ever ever again. They all came and none were labelled with the value, so we didn't know which was which. We loved it up on Amazon and it said to look under \"orders\" to find the serial number for each card and then match it up with the cars to figure it the value. Annoying, but ok, we could do that. Except there were no serial numbers on the website. Or on the app. Or on the receipt from the box. Or anywhere else we looked. We even tried scanning the cards with the app - nope. So I had to call Amazon and wait on hold to talk with someone. That person then couldn't figure out the issue no matter how many ways I explained it, so after quite a while I agreed to talk with a supervisor. On hold again... Finally I got the value of the cards. I had to read off the entire 16 digit serial number of each card to the supervisor in order to get it. She confirmed that there was no other way to have done it.<br />I hope the people on our list enjoy their Amazon cards this year because they will never be getting another one!",
